<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rīdĭcŭlārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		ridiculus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that excites laughter</i>, <i>laughable</i>, <i>droll</i>, <i>funny</i> (ante- and post-class.).—Only as <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rīdĭcŭlārĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>jests</i>, <i>drolleries</i>: ridicularia
			fundere, Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 10</span></i>; cf.
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 2, 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Trin.
				1, 2, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Truc. 3, 2,
			16</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rīdĭcŭlārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a droll</i>,
				<i>a jester</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 4,
				20, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
